  "do_not_say": [
    "A dash on THIS table may be read as 'not included'. Do not generalise this to any other product page - the standing rule elsewhere is that a dash means the source does not say.",
    "Disclose that this is a service, not insurance coverage, and that it pays no benefits. It must never be presented as, or bundled silently into, medical coverage.",
    "Disclose the 3.5% card/ACH processing fee on every sale regardless of which page the client was shown. Do not rely on the panel a given product page happens to display.",
    "Disclose to any client on a tight account that a single failed draft can end the plan.",
    "Do not describe AssistPro, GapSupport, Ameriguard, Prime Health Pass, Express Health Tools or HealthAssist as insurance or as coverage - the portal names each of them a Discount. Do not describe the remaining 36 at all until typed. Do not say 'PPO' about Allstate Dental PPO in a way implying major medical.",
    "Do not tell a client 'the terms are on the page'. Establish which agreement governs their enrolment, and disclose the 3.5% processing fee regardless of which panel their product displays.",
    "Do not tell a client a scheduled benefit amount will be paid in full without qualifying it by the URC limit.",
    "Every recorded verification must cover all four elements. Omitting the recurring monthly amount or the automatic draft is a breach of the platform agreement, not only a compliance risk.",
    "For any product in this group, do not answer a coverage, exclusion, waiting-period or pre-existing question on a recorded call from portal material alone. Obtain the carrier document first.",
    "If asked how the standalone version differs, say the enrolment system does not state a difference. Do not improvise one.",
    "Never describe NEO as the insurance company. Name the carrier for the specific product.",
    "Never type or describe a product from its name. Read the Info page.",
    "Not a source for a service-scope promise on a recorded call.",
    "The monthly cost quoted on a recorded call must include this fee, or the fee must be stated separately before the payment authorisation. Quoting the product page price alone understates what the client will be charged.",
    "Until the PDFs are filed, any compliance challenge to a benefit statement on these products can be answered only with the ledger's citations, not with the underlying document. Treat filing them as outstanding remediation, not housekeeping."
  ],
